- content_for :title, 'Rules'

article.prose
  = link_to 'Back', (request.referer.presence || root_path), class: 'btn btn--small btn--no-border prose__back'
  h1 Rules

  h2 Players
  ul
    li 3 to 20 players. The host sets the limit and runs the big screen but doesn't play.
    li <strong>Insiders</strong> get the secret word. <strong>Imposters</strong> get only a hint.
    li Imposters are picked at random each round, within the range the host chose: at most 1 for every 3 players, and never more than 6.

  h2 A round
  ol
    li Everyone privately looks at their word or hint.
    li The group goes around the table 2, 3, 5 or 7 times, depending on the game settings. Each trip, everyone gives one clue.
    li After each trip there's a discussion (timed or not), then a vote.

  h2 Voting
  ul
    li Vote for any player still in, or Skip. You can change your vote until voting closes.
    li Voting closes when everyone still in has voted, or when the host ends it. Anyone who hasn't voted counts as Skip.
    li The player with the most votes is out. If Skip has the most votes, or there's a tie, nobody is out.
    li Depending on the settings, the big screen either reveals whether the player was an imposter or keeps it secret.
    li Depending on the settings, the big screen either shows who voted for whom or keeps votes anonymous.

  h2 Winning a round
  ul
    li <strong>Insiders win</strong> as soon as every imposter is out. Every Insider scores 1 point, including those voted out.
    li <strong>Imposters win</strong> as soon as it's down to one imposter and one Insider, or only imposters are left.
    li <strong>Imposters also win</strong> if at least one of them is still in after the last trip's vote. Every imposter scores 1 point, including those voted out.
    li Players the host removed from the round don't score that round.

  h2 The game
  ul
    li The host picks 1 to 15 rounds. Every round gets a new word and new imposters, and a word never repeats in the same game.
    li Most points after the last round wins. Ties share the win.
    li Lost your phone? Join again with the same code and the same name, and you'll get your spot back.
